    "body": "**REAL IPHONE SAFARI MANUAL ACCEPTANCE: FAIL on PR #431 exact HEAD `f5c6e90d04109e674918d1041a3f8593049f627c` (2026-10-30). Do not merge.**\n\nOwner tested the isolated physical-iPhone UI lab `https://asynchronia-pr431-ui-lab.raykhalit.workers.dev/` (this test preview suppresses Stage 7.15 and seeds DM / report, but serves the unchanged PR #431 shared UI JS/CSS). Supplied **four real iPhone screenshots**, including one with the *native iOS keyboard*, showing reproducible problems which mocked Chromium's 168/168 did not catch:\n\n1. **DM is squeezed underneath too-large general chat**, especially with the keyboard open. When mobile tab `dm` is active, minimize the pinned *general* chat to its genuine functional minimum (chat header + usable input + resize handle; allow chat log to collapse) and dedicate the available viewport to the **active DM panel**. Preserve/restore user-resized chat height when leaving DM. Respect real `visualViewport` and safe areas; prevent DM and its active editor from disappearing behind keyboard.\n2. **DM conversations should dominate the DM panel**. Current DM tabs/large empty regions/action row crowd out the thread and `#dmInputRow`; make message thread naturally scrollable, keep DM compose input and Send button accessible, give real priority to visible DM content instead of only 88–112px panel floors. With native keyboard, keep the focused editor visible *and usable*, not just technically inside a clipped rectangle. On tiny heights allow other actions to scroll.\n3. **Unwanted long, pale horizontal overlay/track over DM**, visible across nearly the whole width around the input/actions area in two screenshots, highlighted in red. It obstructs the `#dmSend` region and repeats at other DM scroll offsets. **Identify via real DOM elementFromPoint and computed styles before touching CSS** (suspect stray scrollbar/resize/overflow element; do not assume). Remove artifact without disabling legitimate chat resize or tabs.\n4. **Cop report suggestion list invisible** when `#reportInput` is opened on a mobile viewport; screen clipping/keyboard hides choices. `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-dm.js` currently places the appended-to-body `#reportList` at `inputRect.bottom + 4` unconditionally, with fixed position; needs usable above/below placement calculated against `visualViewport`, bounded max-height + independent scroll, reposition on keyboard viewport resize/scroll, focus, and manual DM scroll. Ensure user can tap options and submit without losing focus.\n5. **Already passing:** mobile swipe/tabs **Личка / Баттлы / События**. Do **not** regress or redesign them. Clarification: \"top bar\" for original #431 means the top profile stats/chips/reputation and Menu, **not** these lower tabs. The latter swipe is accepted by owner; no unrelated change requested.\n\n**Code areas to inspect:** `ensureMobilePinnedChatLayout().sync` in `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-core.js`, mirrored `docs/ui/ui-core.js`; relevant `style-base.css` mirrors; existing `ui/ui-dm.js` / `ui/ui-mobile.js` are other potentially owned files: coordinate ownership before modifying them, keep exact Web/docs parity. `#dmLog`, `#dmInputRow`, `#dmExtraRow`, `#reportList`, `#mobilePanelShell`, `#chatResizeHandle`. Current keyboard focus checker treats DM/report and chat alike; chat minimum based on 27% of viewport, starving the DM.\n\n**Required next execution:** same existing Codex workstream/PR #431, inspect current HEAD and ownership locks. Extend actual browser geometry/focus/scroll regression for DM as priority and report list above keyboard, plus track DOM culprit. Re-run all 7 headless sizes, Node/Python, mirrors, CI and independent review. Update same PR only within authorized scope; if `ui-dm.js` is outside current ownership, leave existing file unchanged and clearly request a narrow ownership grant rather than silently expand. **Never claim Safari PASS** until the owner repeats the physical iPhone test after a new exact-HEAD preview. Keep PR OPEN/DRAFT/UNMERGED; no main merge, no deploy over Chat03 or main game.",
